{
  "context": "Keep the normal writer and the observer separate. The writer validates one immutable candidate artifact, obtains one protected github-pages approval, deploys through journal CAS, and issues the signed live receipt. The observer reads the durable head and records retained outcomes. Require an external monitor for independent five-minute observations and ten-minute missing-observation alerting; GitHub Actions scheduling alone does not satisfy that dependency. Use outcome-based evidence for restoration, unknown provider quarantine, and legacy retirement.",
  "description": "Operationalize the simplified publication contract with a scheduled availability observer, full route and DuckDB checks, durable journal reconciliation, retention, and incident evidence. Five-minute observations may report availability, but active transactions and missing observations remain unknown or failed. Full content identity runs hourly and after transactions. The observer cannot deploy, sign, compensate, or finalize.",
